{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "control": "D0"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 126, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none with skip adds a missing input-to-output residual path, whereas replacing an existing op on edge 3 only swaps one direct route for another."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "With edge 1 absent, node 2 depends solely on node 1, so cutting edge 0 disconnects both intermediate nodes and leaves only edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "If edge 5 is none, node 2 never reaches the output, so changing edge 1 has almost no effect."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "A conv on edge 2 only contributes when node 2 feeds the output through edge 5."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing none both creates a node2-to-output path and adds capacity, a bigger gain than replacing an existing op."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without edge 4, removing edge 5 leaves the output fed only by the edge-3 shortcut, collapsing the network."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 4, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a pooling path where none existed is roughly neutral, while swapping out a conv3x3 for pooling loses capacity."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When the edge-3 shortcut is absent, a skip on edge 4 supplies an important shallow gradient path."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a